<div data-class-help>
    <details class="class-help-fallback" data-class-help-fallback>
        <summary>How classes and teacher assignments work</summary>
        <div class="class-help-content" data-class-help-content>
            <section aria-labelledby="class-help-sections"><span class="class-help-icon"><x-icon name="sections" /></span><div><h3 id="class-help-sections">Start with a class and its sections</h3><p>Create <strong>Class 1</strong>, then add sections such as <strong>A</strong> and <strong>B</strong>. The class code is generated from the class name. All sections share the class’s subject list for the selected academic year.</p></div></section>
            <section aria-labelledby="class-help-teachers"><span class="class-help-icon"><x-icon name="teacher" /></span><div><h3 id="class-help-teachers">Two teacher roles</h3><p><strong>Class teacher:</strong> looks after a section. Only one active class teacher can cover a section at a time.</p><p><strong>Subject teacher:</strong> teaches a specific subject, possibly across several classes and sections. The same person can hold both roles.</p></div></section>
            <section aria-labelledby="class-help-subject-column"><span class="class-help-icon"><x-icon name="book" /></span><div><h3 id="class-help-subject-column">Read the Sections list</h3><p><strong>Teacher’s subjects</strong> shows what the class teacher teaches in that section. <strong>Total subjects</strong> counts the class’s subject list. A <strong>Pending</strong> section still needs a class teacher.</p></div></section>
            <section aria-labelledby="class-help-changes"><span class="class-help-icon"><x-icon name="pencil" /></span><div><h3 id="class-help-changes">Choose teachers while editing the class</h3><p>Open a class → <strong>Edit class</strong> → <strong>Teachers</strong>. Select a class teacher for each section. For each subject, choose one teacher for all sections or use different teachers by section.</p><p>Choosing a replacement updates the selected sections when you <strong>Save class</strong>. Previous assignments remain in history.</p></div></section>
            <aside class="class-help-example" aria-labelledby="class-help-example"><h3 id="class-help-example">For example</h3><p>Ms. Pooja is the class teacher for <strong>Class 1 · Section A</strong>. She can also teach <strong>Mathematics in Class 2 · Section B</strong> through a separate subject assignment.</p></aside>
            <p class="class-help-note"><x-icon name="calendar" /><span>Teacher and subject assignments belong to an academic year. Use an active current year when setting them up from a class.</span></p>
        </div>
    </details>
    <dialog id="class-help-dialog" class="student-workflow-dialog class-help-dialog" data-class-help-dialog aria-labelledby="class-help-heading" aria-describedby="class-help-description">
        <div class="student-modal-header"><div><h2 id="class-help-heading" tabindex="-1">Classes &amp; teacher assignments</h2><p id="class-help-description">A quick guide to setting up your classes.</p></div><button type="button" class="icon-button" data-class-help-close aria-label="Close class setup guide"><x-icon name="close" /></button></div>
        <div class="student-modal-content" data-class-help-slot></div>
        <div class="student-modal-footer"><button type="button" class="button-primary" data-class-help-close>Got it</button></div>
    </dialog>
</div>
